WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is very exciting.
You're traveling around with

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Monty Python
and the Holy Grail,"

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.038 line:92%
a personal favorite of mine.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so people
love this movie now.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was not a joy to make,
though.

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:08.775 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Is that accurate?

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, it was miserable.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.880 line:92%
It was Scotland in April,

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the weather in Scotland
is really bad

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
except for two weeks
in September.

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:22.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And we were just miserable.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:22.856 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We were wet.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:24.124 line:92%
We got on the mountainside

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:27.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
with that strange chainmail
with knitted string.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:30.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
And after about 10 minutes,
it would start to rain,

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we could afford
about three umbrellas.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:36.269
I mean,
the film was made for $400,000.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's crazy.
-Crazy.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:42.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, the interesting thing
is it looks beautiful

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.576 line:92%
because Scotland looks old.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:47.447 size:84% position:42%
So it looks accurate
to what you were doing.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.114 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And the castle --

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:52.886
we were only allowed to film in
this one castle, Doune Castle.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:54.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we tried to film
everywhere else.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
They said, "Oh, no, you can't
have comedy here.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:00.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's real history here.
You can't do comedy."

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:02.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is now a tourist spot.
-Really?

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:03.263 size:88% position:44% line:92%
The actual Monty Python?

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Doune Castle,
the actual Monty Python,

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
attracts tourists
from all over the world.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:08.435 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's so funny.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.570
And you did have to come up with
some inventive things

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.605
that people probably credited as
comedy writing,

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:15.475
but were actually done out of
necessity for your budget.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:18.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like the actual coconuts
for the horses.

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:18.445 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:20.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys couldn't afford
horses. Is that true?

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, that's --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:24.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is why Michael Palin,
bless him,

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
came up with the idea
of the coconuts, you see.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's so funny.
-You know it is that --

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
Necessity is
the mother of invention.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:34.561
Sometimes you don't have much
and you have to improvise.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:37.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's sometimes when the very
best ideas come through.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you ever --
So, "Monty Python,"

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:39.532 line:92%
you made that for $400,000,

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was your first one
of your movies.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes?
-Yes.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.204
-Did they start giving you more
money for the other movies

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:45.105 line:92%
or were they always shoestring?

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:48.775 size:84% position:42%
-Well, then after that,
we did "Life of Brian,"

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:51.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this extraordinary --
[ Applause ]

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, please.
-Thank you.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.815 line:92%
This is an extraordinary story.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:02:00.019 size:81% position:41%
We couldn't get anyone
to give us ££2 million

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.154 size:88% position:44% line:92%
to make "Life of Brian."

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:03.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it took a fortune.
-Yeah.

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:04.190 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-We couldn't get anyone.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:08.161
And we went 'round to England
and then we came to the studios

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:10.663 line:92%
here in Hollywood and New York,

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.298 size:84% position:42%
and nobody was prepared
to put the money up.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:15.635
-Was it because they didn't --
But was it because about the --

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.536 line:92%
that it was about religion,

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:18.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
or just they didn't think
it would work?

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:20.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I don't think that
at that point

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was so much of a problem.
-Oh, funny.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.210
-But then the most extraordinary
thing is,

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:24.911 line:92%
Eric Idle rang us all up.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:28.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd already made arrangements
to do a movie in Vienna

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.048 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
with Peter Sellers

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:31.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I thought it wasn't
going to happen.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:31.918 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:35.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Eric said,
"The movie is on."

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:37.190 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And we said, "W-W-Why?"

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:41.594
And he said, "George Harrison is
putting the money up."

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:42.028 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow!

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He knew George --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:45.398 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Yeah. He knew George.

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:51.571
He gave George the script, and
George rang him up the next day

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:54.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
and said
"I'm putting the money up."

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:54.707 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Eric said, "What are you
talking about?"

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:58.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said,
"I'll put the money up."

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's amazing.
-And Eric said, "Why?"

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:05.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
And dear George said,
"I want to see the movie."

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:07.387 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:09.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
Isn't that amazing?
[ Applause ]

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:11.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
-I know.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:12.292 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So I mean -- you know,

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:14.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's the best film
Python ever made.

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:18.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wouldn't have been made if it
wasn't for George Harrison.

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:21.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, oh, my goodness.
God bless is right.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.135 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
You do a Q&amp;A
when you show this film.

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:25.238 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yes.

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:27.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And what sort of questions do
people ask you?

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:29.375 size:75% position:38%
-That's what I love,
is you don't know.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
You see, when you do
your one-man show

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:34.881
you say pretty much the same as
you said the previous night.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if it's a great audience
you have a good time,

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:42.288
and if it's a slow audience
like El Paso -- hint, hint --

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:46.793 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:50.563
You wonder at the end whether
they're going to kill you.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:51.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:53.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they're very nice
and they clap.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that was their way of
enjoying it.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:57.103 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.239
I do like -- It's nice to engage
with people.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you do your Q&amp;A
at the end or --

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:02.709 line:92%
-Yes. I do it at the end.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:04.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
You never know
what they're gonna ask.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:08.014
I mean, when I was doing it
with Eric a couple of years ago,

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:11.651
one -- one quite young, very
attractive woman said to Eric,

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:14.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What is your favorite
sexual position?"

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:15.455 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:18.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought, "How is he going to
get out of that?"

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.326 line:92%
And without batting an eyelid,

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.862
Eric said,
"Oh, the male marital position.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:27.400
That's the man flat on his back
with his wallet wide open."

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.002 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:34.007
But the strangest one, I mean
the one that totally broke me up

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:36.809 line:92%
was in -- It was in Florida,

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:41.180
and a lady, rather smartly
dressed, middle-aged lady,

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.649 line:92%
but very smart, got up and said,

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:45.752
"Mr. Idle, Mr. Cleese, may I ask
you a serious question?"

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:46.319 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Of course."

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:51.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
She said,
"Did the Queen kill Diana?"

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:56.663 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.663 --> 00:05:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:06.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
2,000 people there all went...
[ Gasps ]

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:06.873 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:09.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was the only
one laughing.

00:05:09.342 --> 00:05:10.376 size:88% position:44% line:92%
You know, I was floored.

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:13.179
In the end, I had time to think
and I said,

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:16.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, certainly not with
her bare hands."

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:16.849 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:20.620
But it's great when you don't
know what's going to happen.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.154 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I love that.

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:22.822 line:92%
-You also -- Every now and then

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:25.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
somebody will walk out
of your show.

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:27.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-And you celebrate that.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.829
-Well, I think it's very brave.
-Yeah.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:32.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know?
Because after all, most --

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:34.600 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
Most Python fans
aren't Trump fans.

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:37.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's face it.
-Yeah.

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:40.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's true.
There's not a lot of --

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:41.374 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:43.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And if I --
if I do a Trump joke,

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
sometimes you can see
somebody go...

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:49.115 size:88% position:44%
and they get up and they
walk out to the aisle.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I say,
"Was it the Trump joke?"

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:54.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
And sometimes they say "Yes!"
or sometimes they go...

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:57.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And I think that's great.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
I say, "Please,
a round of applause

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:00.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
for this very,
very brave person."

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:01.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they get
a nice round of applause.

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:03.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's nice.
-Yeah, it's nice.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:05.698
-You just don't let that catch
on or else people are gonna just

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
start leaving just for the
applause, you know.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.435
You don't want that getting out.
-True.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.270
-It's always such a pleasure to
see you.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for coming back.

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:14.540
-Thank you for having me.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:17.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Come soon.
Don't stay away this long.

